course: dictionary
lesson: 15640
title: One word, two meanings: terminus
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A terminus is the last stop on a bus, train or tram route. «The bus goes all the way to the terminus, so everyone must get off.» The word tells you where the journey ends. Terminus is a noun, so it names a place.
explain: The word can also mean an end point or limit, in a more formal way. «The project reached its terminus when the money ran out.» Nothing here is a bus stop. It means the point where something finishes. Use context to choose: is the sentence about a vehicle or route, or about something coming to an end?
explain: The plural can be termini or terminuses. «The trains leave from two termini in the city.» Both plurals are correct, and termini is the more formal one. Check the sentence: if it fits a bus or train, it is probably the travel meaning.
fact: A terminus is the last stop or station at the end of a bus, train or tram route.
fact: A terminus can also be an end point or limit of something; this is a formal use.
fact: The plural of terminus can be termini or terminuses.
fact: Phrases you may hear are «bus terminus» and «the end of the line», which both mean the last stop.
fact: On a maths journey, you count the stops up to the terminus.
exercise: «The driver called out, "This is the terminus, everybody off!"» What is the terminus? | The middle of the town | The driver's seat | *The last stop on the route | The first stop on the route
exercise: Which word means the last stop at the end of a bus or train route? | Platform | Ticket | *Terminus | Junction
exercise: Ella says, «The project reached its terminus.» What does terminus mean here? | A ticket office | A bus stop in the middle of a route | *An end point or limit | The start of something
test: A tram starts at stop 1 and its terminus is stop 9. How many stops are there after stop 1 up to the terminus? | *8 | 10 | 9 | 7
test: Which is a correct plural of terminus? | Terminis | *Termini | Terminies | Terminuss
exam: Ben says, «The train terminus is at the end of the line.» What is the terminus? | A ticket machine | *The last station at the end of the line | The train's engine | The first station on the line
